1689: | 0.1 | 2026-09-29 | Initial specification. |
1690: | 0.2 | 2026-09-30 | Following `spec-critical-evaluation.md` and a re-check of the Antigravity built-in docs:<br>• Pipeline runs as Antigravity scheduled sidecars (periodic ticks); no daemon or socket.<br>• Capture moved to a transcript sweep, with `Stop` as a nudge and no `PostToolUse` capture hook.<br>• Recursion guard for pipeline-created conversations.<br>• Pluggable LLM backends (`api` / `agentapi`).<br>• Two-lane publish and review profiles.<br>• Delivery hook latency budget and compiled-hook option; degraded modes.<br>• Two-tier déjà-vu detection (immediate lexical match in the hook, semantic check on a 1-minute tick).<br>• Map loaded via an `AGENTS.md`/`CLAUDE.md` include.<br>• `memory.stats` and an observability layer.<br>• Entity-extraction exactness and subsystem bootstrap; month-sharded claims and scale estimate.<br>• B5 extraction-precision benchmark and P1 gates with a fallback; P0 experiments E1–E6; P0.5 episode search.<br>• Transcript location and format resolved (Q4). |
1691: | 0.3 | 2026-09-30 | Execution model settled with the user:<br>• Two invocation paths with strictly separate jobs: hooks read, inject and spool; the scheduled tick does all asynchronous work. Harness-level, not OS-level; no detached processes.<br>• Durable job table advanced across ticks, with leases, idempotency keys, budgets and a circuit breaker.<br>• One-minute tick; the watcher sidecar folded into it.<br>• All LLM work runs on the user's Antigravity quota: housekeeping via headless `agy -p` (measured at ~17k tokens of fixed overhead and ~13 s per call, so items are batched per call); no API key.<br>• Session visibility policy: repo work and reports in the IDE; housekeeping headless.<br>• Weekly review report as an IDE conversation carrying gap questions, pending claims and proposed work; human replies captured as evidence.<br>• LLM stages defined as pure functions.<br>• `PreToolUse` gate-once delivery for risky actions and déjà-vu.<br>• Capture sweep extended to the Antigravity CLI store.<br>• Publishing through a dedicated git worktree.<br>• Experiments revised (E7 isolation, E10 overhead, E11 quota). |
1692: | 0.4 | 2026-09-30 | Claude Code support and external review:<br>• P13 evidence independence with per-step exposure markers and author classification; independence rules in extraction and reconcile.<br>• Report-reply mechanism (§9.2.1).<br>• §4.4.1 cost model from measured Antigravity transcript sizes; salience windows and packing; the fixed overhead identified as dominating small interactive calls.<br>• Déjà-vu reframed as tier 0 (proactive) / tier 1 (lexical safety net, generated match blocks) / tier 2 (late correction; seconds on Claude Code via `asyncRewake`).<br>• §12.2 rewritten from verified Claude Code docs: hook mapping, `claude -p --safe-mode` executor, Desktop scheduled task reports, async-hook tick triggers, transcript parser policy, auto-memory coexistence, experiments C1–C7.<br>• Native-floor degraded mode.<br>• §17 implementation decisions (D1 open, recommendation: one compiled binary; D2 and D3 decided).<br>• P0 extended to both harnesses; P2 builds a normalised event model, Antigravity first. |
1693: | 0.5 | 2026-09-30 | Harness-neutral techniques from a review of Claude Code auto memory (Claude-specific notes in `docs/claude_architecture.md` §4.7):<br>• Claims gain `relevant_when` (for selection) and `apply` (for action) lines; pushes render `apply`.<br>• Claim index view per subsystem, so agents can walk MAP → index → claim with plain reads; used as the fallback when task linking fails and in degraded modes.<br>• Every pushed claim carries a currency stamp; the hook checks that anchored files exist.<br>• `open-issue` claims carry `closes_when` conditions evaluated by the tick; new `resolved` status; unknown closure means pull-only.<br>• Writes to memory artefacts (PA files, harness-native stores) and approval signals are triage keep rules; written text kept as `note` steps, leads rather than evidence.<br>• Over-budget views are re-synthesised rather than truncated.<br>• Extraction reports referenced `gaps`, which feed coverage. |
1694: | 0.6 | 2026-09-30 | User decisions:<br>• **Release order:** Release 1 targets Antigravity; Release 2 adds Claude Code (D4). Claude Code-specific text is tagged **[R2]**; build phases split into §15.1 (P0–P5) and §15.2 (R2.1–R2.3), with Release 2 able to start after P2.<br>• **Go** (D1): one cgo-free binary with `hook`, `tick`, `mcp`, `install` and operator subcommands (§18.1); a package layout with an enforced core/adapter boundary (§18.2); harness interfaces and capability-based delivery (§18.3); libraries (§18.4); hook fast path (§18.5); portability rules for Release 1 (§18.6), including a recommended sweep-only copy of Claude Code transcripts from P0.<br>• Plugin files generated by `repo-memory install` with absolute paths; D2 and D3 scoped to Release 1. |
1695: | 0.7 | 2026-10-01 | From the programme-plan review: repository enrolment (`repo-memory init`/`leave`, registry, hooks no-op within 5 ms outside enrolled workspaces, sweep scoped to enrolled repositories) and a kill switch (`REPO_MEMORY_DISABLED`, `enabled: false`, `enable`/`disable`) in §4.6; machine configuration and registry in §5.6; new subcommands in §18.1; Q24. |
1696: | 0.8 | 2026-10-01 | Third-party review (issue #1), verified against the runtime:<br>• Antigravity transcript file set and `truncated_fields` resolution (§6.2, E12); incremental transcript copying.<br>• Template-safe repo ID and per-clone publishing worktrees (§4.6, §5.6).<br>• Decision-marker salience windows (§6.4); mechanical P13 precondition (§6.6).<br>• `gate-once` limited to irreversible actions; E9 widened (§7.5); tier-1 reasoning check at `PreToolUse` (§7.6).<br>• Sidecar permissions, dashboard enablement and `model_decision` native rules (§12.1, E2/E4/E6 updated).<br>• SQLite concurrency and Windows-safe index swap (§18.4).<br>• Cost estimates flagged as lower bounds pending full-transcript measurement (§4.4.1). |
